    "Daddy’s laptop was ringing. On the screen, in cheerful letters, it said: MUMMY.",
    "Daddy went the colour of cold porridge. “Oh dear,” he said. “Oh dear, oh dear, oh DEAR! If Mummy sees you here, I shall be in more trouble than any man has ever been in, in the entire history of trouble. Hide! *Hide!*”",
    "Oscar, who was good at following instructions when they were sensible, slid under the bed with his football in a single smooth movement, like a letter going under a door. Samuel, who was good at following instructions when they were exciting, hurled himself behind the long velvet curtains, taking Roary with him and leaving a faint trail of syrup.",
    "Daddy smoothed his hair, arranged his face into what he imagined was a natural expression, and pressed ANSWER.",
    "There was Mummy, in the kitchen at home, with the grey English afternoon in the window behind her. Beside her stood Victoria, holding Rosie, who was wearing most of a banana.",
