    "“I,” he declared, “am SAMUEL LIGHTNING THUNDERBOLT FIRE THE KNIGHT! And I am in AMERICA!”",
    "For a moment, nobody in England said anything at all. Mummy’s mouth fell open. Victoria’s eyebrows rose. Rosie clapped, delighted to be proved right at last. Then Mummy’s eyebrows came down — slowly, like the drawbridge of a very cross castle — and she said, in a voice that rattled the laptop speakers:",
    "“**DADDY!**”",
    "“It wasn’t me!” squeaked Daddy. “I didn’t know! They were in the *suitcases*! I thought I’d packed a rhinoceros!”",
    "Oscar slid out from under the bed and stood up beside his brother, very straight, the way he did when he had to own up to something. “It’s true, Mummy,” he said. “Daddy didn’t know. It was my plan. Granny doesn’t know about the sleepover, either. I’m sorry we didn’t tell you.” He took a breath. “But we missed Daddy before he’d even gone. And now something enormous has happened. The Golden Gate Bridge has disappeared in the night — the whole thing — and we think we can help find it.”",
    "Mummy looked at her two sons for a long moment: safe, and sticky, and standing in a hotel room on the other side of the world with their chins up. Something in her face softened, and her eyebrows rose again, a little.",
    "“Well,” she said at last. “I am still very cross. *Very.* But I suppose you can’t exactly post yourselves home. So you may stay until the end of the trip — on one strict condition. You *look after Daddy.* He worries, you know.”",
    "“We know,” said both boys together.",
    "“And you call me every single day.”",
    "“We PROMISE!”",
    "“It’s awfully quiet here without you, anyway,” Mummy admitted. “No sword fights at all.”",
