    "q": "The three passengers each said something about the purple-coat man:\n• The pug lady: “He went downhill, towards the water.”\n• The burrito man: “The pug lady is fibbing — he went uphill.”\n• The skateboard girl: “The burrito man is fibbing.”\nExactly ONE of them was fibbing. Without using what Big Lou saw, can you prove who it was?",
    "a": "The burrito man. If the pug lady were fibbing, the burrito man would be truthful — so the skateboard girl would be fibbing too, making two fibbers; and if the skateboard girl were fibbing, the burrito man would be truthful, so the pug lady would be fibbing too — two again. Only one possibility leaves exactly one fibber: the burrito man (which also fits what Big Lou saw)."
