    "“This is the oldest Chinatown in North America,” said Oscar, who had read it in a book called *Cities of the World* and had read it again, twice, because he liked the bit about the earthquake. “People have lived here since the Gold Rush. It burned down in 1906, and they built it all back up again, even more beautiful.”",
